  "lore": "To classify the Archmage as a mere mortal is a folly that has filled many a pauper\u2019s grave. These entities dwell within \"Sanctums\"\u2014impossible spires that pierce the firmament or shimmering folds in reality where time flows like cooling wax.\n\nIn the ecology of the arcane, the Archmage is an apex scavenger of the ethereal. They do not hunt for meat, but for *resonance*. Their predatory behavior is subtle: they cast nets of complex ritual to ensnare wandering spirits or the very threads of causality. Most perilous is their habit of luring the ambitious; an Archmage \"feeds\" by harvesting the raw potential of apprentices, consuming their vitality to fuel another century of isolation.\n\nLocal folklore dubs them the \"Hollow Kings.\" In the taverns of the High Marches, it is whispered that an Archmage has traded their soul for a mirror of the cosmos. To encounter one is to stand before a living storm\u2014a creature that has forgotten the warmth of the sun in favor of the cold brilliance of the stars. Tread lightly, for to them, you are but a flickering candle in a library of eternal shadows.",
